# PART 1 — PROJECT IDENTITY

## 1.1 Application Name

Xer0byte

## 1.2 Product Type

An Android-first, WhatsApp-inspired, peer-to-peer offline messaging application.

## 1.3 Existing Repository

GitHub repository:

https://github.com/Xer0byte/Xer0byte-App

Repository owner: Xer0byte

Application name: Xer0byte

## 1.4 Main Objective

Build a messaging application that allows users to communicate with nearby compatible devices without requiring:

- Internet access
- Mobile data
- Wi-Fi internet access
- A central messaging server
- Cloud authentication
- Online message synchronization
- Push notification services for core messaging
- A remote database for core messaging

The primary communication method should be direct Bluetooth communication.

The application must work when two compatible Android phones are physically near each other, have Bluetooth enabled, have granted the required permissions, and establish a supported connection.

The application should remain useful when internet access is unavailable.

## 1.5 Product Vision

Xer0byte should combine the familiar experience of a modern messaging application with the independence of offline communication.

The user should be able to:

1. Open the application.
2. Set up a local profile.
3. Discover nearby compatible devices.
4. Connect to another user.
5. Exchange real text messages.
6. Receive replies.
7. View timestamps and message delivery states.
8. Reopen previous conversations.
9. Retain chat history after restarting the application.
10. Recover gracefully when Bluetooth connectivity is interrupted.
11. Transfer supported files when that feature has been implemented.
12. Manage trusted devices, privacy, permissions, and storage.

The application must prioritize reliable core functionality over a large number of incomplete features.

